led="true" focusable="false" focused="false" scrollable="false" long-clickable="false" password="false" selected="false" bounds="[52,495][1028,575]" /><node index="1" text="You're on the latest version (2.5.19). Here's what's in it:" resource-id="" class="android.widget.TextView" package="com.obdreader.app" content-desc="" checkable="false" checked="false" clickable="false" enabled="true" focusable="false" focused="false" scrollable="false" long-clickable="false" password="false" selected="false" bounds="[52,575][1028,666]" /><node index="2" text="2.5.19  ·  27 November 2026" resource-id="" class="android.widget.TextView" package="com.obdreader.app" content-desc="" checkable="false" checked="false" clickable="false" enabled="true" focusable="false" focused="false" scrollable="false" long-clickable="false" password="false" selected="false" bounds="[52,666][1028,782]" /><node index="3" text="• More maker codes for Hyundai, Genesis and Kia. 32 more manufacturer-specific codes, each explained only for the models, years and engines the maker's own service bulletin names. Hyundai: the 12-volt lithium battery code on the Elantra, Sonata and Tucson hybrids, the electric oil pump codes for the 8-speed dual-clutch gearbox (Santa Fe, Sonata and Santa Cruz 2.5 turbo, and the Elantra N, Kona N and Veloster N), the charging unit (ICCU) codes on the Ioniq 5 and Ioniq 6, and drive battery codes on the Kona Electric. Genesis: the charging unit code on the GV60. Kia: the 12-volt lithium battery code on the Niro and Sportage hybrids, charging unit codes on the EV6 and EV9, a battery heater relay code on the Niro EV, a CVT learning code on the Cerato, Soul and Seltos 2.0, an oil pump code for the Sorento and K5 2.5 turbo, and purge hose and generator belt codes on the Sorento hybrid.&#10;• More maker codes for Subaru. 8 more Subaru codes, each explained only for the models and years Subaru's own service bulletins and technician newsletters name: a generator code on the 2014 XV (Crosstrek) hybrid, a blocked EVAP system code on petrol Imprezas, XVs (Crosstreks), Foresters, WRXs and Ascents, a direct-injection air-fuel imbalance code on the 2017–2019 BRZ, lost contact with the door mirror modules on the 2020 Liberty (Legacy) and Outback, a stuck passenger air mix door on the 2020–2021 Liberty (Legacy) and Outback, lost contact with EyeSight on the 2020 Impreza and Ascent, and a charging communication code on the Solterra.&#10;• Clearer Santa Fe hybrid purge hose code. Hyundai's P1441 explanation no longer says which side of the purge valve the loose hose is on, because Hyundai's bulletin calls it the rear hose without saying which side that is." resource-id="" class="android.widget.TextView" package="com.obdreader.app" content-desc="" checkable="false" checked="false" clickable="false" enabled="true" focusable="false" focused="false" scrollable="false" long-clickable="false" password="false" selected="false" bounds="[52,782][1028,2264]" /></node></node></node></node></node></node></node></node></node></node></hierarchy>